==Strategy==
This is a tough stage. The combination of Cafeteria's constant curses, Mega Baa Baa constantly juggling attackers, Li'l Doges terrorising the cats with their annoying dodge, and Great angel Chibinel's constant support along with Camelle, the Army really puts up a fight. The ideal Meatshield here is [[Rocker Cat (Rare Cat)|Ramen Cat]], preferably with Resist Curse, as a high level Ramen Cat can survive 2 hits from Cafeteria and is Resistant against Angels, those of which are a common threat in this stage. Start off the stage by saving up all your money to get to max worker level, and using preferably Talented [[Hip Hop Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Can Can Cat]] with Double Bounty unlocked to kill off the Gabriels and Heavenly Hippoe. As for the two Mega Baa Baas, Spam Meatshields to take care of them while using Can Can and [[Express Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Bullet Train]] to kill them quickly.

Upon hitting the base, your main focus isn't surviving, but killing the first Cafeteria Cat as soon as possible, or else a second one will appear to make it more difficult to win. A spam of Ramen Cat and [[Crazed Tank Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Manic Eraser]] can stall all the enemies easily, but if the two aren't at a high enough level, a Research Combo like [[Bony Bone (Combo)|Bony Bone]] and [[Biohazard (Combo)|Biohazard]] should be considered, although the spamming may dip into your cash a bit more. [[Slime Cat (Rare Cat)|Jelly Dumpling Cat]] is heavily recommended to deal with Chibinel and Camelle, his level 7 waves can hinder everyone on the field (Pre-True Form is usable, but not as effectively), use him during Cafeteria's downtime between attacks to snipe the backliners. [[Vaulter Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Housewife Cat]] or a high level [[Lizard Cat (Normal Cat)|King Dragon]]/[[Crazed Lizard Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Manic King Dragon Cat]] can help chip away at Cafeteria, and a strong long ranged attacker like [[Urs & Fenrir (Special Cat)|Urs & Fenrir]] can aid immensely. Awakened Bahamut Cat can especially help here, being able to take off 1/17th of Cafeteria's hp per hit and is able to survive a hit at level 30, albeit with very little HP left. If you have Bahamut's Explosion Talent, he becomes significantly more powerful and can chip off nearly 25% of Cafeteria's hp, and can nuke all the peons while still managing to hit the main threat.

Once the second Cafeteria Cat has spawned, you are in the final stretch of the fight. By this point, your Bahamut Cat should have recharged, and you should have good enough money to spam your meatshields. By this point, the only enemies spawning are the Li'l Doges, the Last Chibinel and Heavenly Hippoes, so you can take a breather. You can perform the same strategy of Meatshield & Attacker until Cafeteria dies. Once that happens, you effectively win.

